message:
tools: selftune.py prices on the A6 chain model, holds out whole sessions, writes a spec that matches the preset (item 70)

The 2026-11-09 dry run (+8.6% candidate profile, +23.1% with k-th miss) used time_ceiling.window_ms serial with promotions
free: the model A6 refuted (k-th miss +14% modeled against +2.0% +-1.6 measured).  Now:
- chain_model.py: time_ceiling.window_ms2 with the --validate constants as one function (deferral and FUSE_PHASES from the
  base config's env, promotion DMA costs CPU time);
- held-out folds: leave one session out, or k contiguous blocks of one session; a policy goes on only with mean >= --min-gain
  and >= --min-positive of the folds gaining, and >= --min-windows decode windows; prompt windows (> 16 rows) are dropped;
- the candidate ranks every pair (a short ranking caps the cache, issue #46);
- the A/B spec uses the fast-hip base, the blocking tier (no --adapt-async, which was rejected), cases short + edit, lossy
  (placement moves work between GPU and CPU kernels).
On the recorded 219-window trace, 4 blocks: candidate profile +4.6% mean (-2.5 .. +11.5, 3 of 4 blocks gain) goes on;
k-th miss +2.0 / +2.7% (1 of 4 blocks gains) does not.  12 python tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

bench: replay_turns.py, agent-traffic replay for the conversation-cache arms (TEST_PLAN 4.1)

abtest's cases are one-shot requests, so they never park a long conversation or evict it with a side request.
replay_turns.py replays one recorded session of pancake-turns.jsonl (sizes and timing only) as streamed chat
requests against a fresh server per arm of an abtest spec (abtest start_server / quiet_gate / NoiseMonitor /
make_config; the run's engine log and turn log go to the out directory):
- conversations split by prompt growth, so a re-read with reused == 0 stays in its conversation (the cold
  re-read the cache arms should turn warm); smaller requests are side requests, repeated texts where reused > 0;
- each agent turn = the previous messages + the reply the server returned + a <tool_response> message sized to
  the recorded prompt_total (within 2 tokens, counted with the server's own tokenizer and template imported
  locally; usage.prompt_tokens corrects any offset); text = the repo's C++ sources, deterministic;
- recorded output length and thinking on/off, greedy, think time capped (--max-gap);
- per request: prompt tokens, reused (engine line), prompt time, TTFT, decode tok/s, park/skip/restore/evict;
  per arm: cold re-reads, total prompt / turn time, peak RSS, lowest MemAvailable, auto budget line;
  verdict on total prompt time (paired 95% interval with --reps >= 2, else deltas);
- --synthetic (4.0.1 shape without the log), --session window|sN|id, --list-sessions, --scale, --dry-run.
Spec 11 gets a "replay" block (the 11-09 16:13-16:43 session, base vs cache2048-min8192, optional base1280).
Dry runs only (no server, no GPU): log session 75 requests, all built within 2 tokens, ~13.5 min per arm;
synthetic 48 requests, 6.2-9.4 min per arm. test_replay_turns.py: split, repeats, sizing, engine lines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
